            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we need to do some amount of testing that the object_path escaping is working properly?  Invent some injected character names possibly?\n\nI don't need to hold it up here, but it's been a problem in the past that was worked around.  This should arguably have the same behavior."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> that the object_path escaping is working properly?  I\n\nobject_path escaping is tested in sdbusplus unit tests. I did not encounter any issues with it.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/sdbusplus/blob/master/test/message/types.cpp\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/sdbusplus/blob/master/test/message/native_types.cpp\n\nI don't think EM needs to do anything special here that's not already covered by (sdbusplus) unit tests but if that's the case then we should probably add those unit tests.\n\n> Invent some injected character names possibly?\n\nWhich edge case are we talking about? Which code path / function ? Can you give an example.\n\n> I don't need to hold it up here,\n\nalright, i will mark it as resolved but we should probably clarify the cases you were worried about"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "One very minor copy/construction thing, then LGTM."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 380,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "?  This is already an object_path, and we're making a copy, shouldn't this just be \"path\" ?\n\nIn very old compilers the explicit construction was required (i forget the details) but these days we can just do the simple thing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/dbus_interface.cpp",
                    "line": 380,
                    "reviewer": {
